# Local-only testing (QuickerPay)

**Hard rule.** Every test, smoke, browser session, seed, health check, and self-provision write uses **this machine only**. Loopback hosts only.

`test` VPS and `*.safepay247.com` are **not** a testing target. Deploy/ops there only when the user explicitly orders that ops work in the same chat — never as smoke, browser QA, or sign-off proof.

## Allowed targets

| Piece | Allowed |
| --- | --- |
| Web | `http://demo.quickerpay.local:3000` (or another `*.quickerpay.local` that resolves to `127.0.0.1`). Never a deployed URL. |
| API | `http://127.0.0.1:4000` or `http://localhost:4000` only |
| Postgres | `QP_CONTROL_DB_HOST` and `QP_TENANT_DB_HOST` are `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` only |
| Redis | `REDIS_URL` host is `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` only |

## Banned test targets (always)

Do **not** use any of these for smokes, browser MCP, agentic QA, seeds, or health proofs:

- `*.safepay247.com` — including `test.`, `testapi.`, `exchange.`, production CRM
- VPS IP `178.94.251.176` (SSH/`curl` for testing)
- App Platform / DigitalOcean / Vercel production or preview as a QA API/DB
- Any non-loopback host for web, API, Postgres, or Redis

If the user asks to “smoke on VPS / test.safepay247.com / exchange”: **stop**. Report **Blocked**. Tell them to use the local stack only.

## Before the first request

Prove all four pieces are local. Read the local `.env` for DB and Redis hosts — do **not** print secrets. Confirm Redis answers (`PING`) and Postgres accepts a connection on those local hosts.

If any host, IP, or cloud URL is remote: **stop**. Report Blocked. Do **not** switch env files to a remote target to “make the test run.” Do **not** fall back to production, App Platform, staging, hosted Postgres, or hosted Redis.

## Builds

`pnpm run build`, API compile, and unit tests run on this machine. They do **not** deploy.

## Ops exception (not testing)

SSH, rsync deploy, or remote wipe only when the user **explicitly** orders that ops work in that chat. That is not a Definition-of-Done substitute and must not include smoke/browser against the VPS.

## Forbidden

- Any non-loopback API, web, database, or Redis for testing
- Committing `.env`, passwords, TOTP secrets, or scratch seeds
- Using a remote stack because the local stack is down
- Treating “test env” / `QP_ENV=test` on the VPS as an allowed agentic QA target

